          "severity": "blocking",
          "location": "results/research/issue120/trees/round_20261025_021934_521/train_graph_denoised_residual/PROPOSAL.json:1",
          "detail": "There is no trainer or model code in the designated tree, so a real forward/backward pass cannot be run or inspected there. No evidence in this tree establishes finite losses/gradients, parameter reachability, or stable optimizer behavior.",
          "reproduction": "The tree file listing contains no Python files, and therefore no importable trainer/model entry point.",
          "correction": "Include the actual trainer and its model dependencies in the target tree and exercise a finite forward/backward step on a representative minibatch, checking intended trainable parameters receive finite nonzero gradients."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "integration",
      "verdict": "NEEDS_FIX",
      "findings": [
        {
          "severity": "blocking",
          "location": "results/research/issue120/trees/round_20261025_021934_521/train_graph_denoised_residual/PROPOSAL.json:1",
          "detail": "The designated tree has no trainer entry point, model package, launcher, or export implementation, so the real trainer, frozen data path, SID indexing/export, and distributed launcher cannot be verified or run from it.",
          "reproduction": "`find` the designated tree: the only file is PROPOSAL.json. The separate implementation artifact's train_rqvae.py imports `from model import RQVAE`, but no `model/` package is included in that artifact's listed tree either, so running that script as delivered cannot resolve the dependency.",
          "correction": "Deliver a self-contained implementation tree with the unchanged baseline model/runtime dependencies and correct frozen train input, then run the actual entry point (including the supported torchrun path) and validate exported SID row-to-item indexing and uniqueness against the baseline consumer contract."
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "location": "results/research/issue120/rounds/round_20261025_021934_521/agents/implementation_train_graph_denoised_residual/tree/train_rqvae.py:77",
          "detail": "The available implementation fixes GRAPH_LAMBDA to 0.1 and explicitly leaves validation-based lambda selection downstream, but the specified experiment compares lambda in {0.1, 0.3, 0.5} under a predeclared validation protocol. The delivered trainer cannot perform that comparison, and this fixed choice is not supported by the stated selection protocol.",
          "reproduction": "Inspect GRAPH_LAMBDA and its only use at lines 77 and 263: the sole executed graph transformation always uses 0.1; there is no candidate loop or validation selection in the script.",
          "correction": "Implement the declared candidate runs/selection using the predeclared validation protocol, or explicitly scope this artifact as one candidate only and do not claim the full specified experiment/integration is complete."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
EOF

